🔹 Algorithm
Step 1: Insert New Interval
Traverse all intervals.
Insert the new interval before the first interval whose start is greater than or equal to it.
Use a flag to ensure it is inserted only once.
If not inserted during traversal, add it at the end.
Step 2: Merge Intervals
Initialize start1 and end1 from the first interval.
Traverse remaining intervals:
If overlapping (end1 >= start2):
Merge → end1 = max(end1, end2)
Else:
Add previous interval to result
Update start1, end1
Add the last interval to result.
Complexity:
Time Complexity=O(n)
Space Complexity=O(n) (extra list used for insertion and result)
